On Sat, 2003-08-16 at 02:21, Brown, Len wrote:
> I've seen a similar problem when booting new kernels on top of Red Hat.
> 
> Look in /boot/grub/menu.* and see what root is set to.
> Don't use the LABEL thingie, use the real device, eg root=/dev/sda2

I use the prompt of GRUB that is:
root (hd0,2)
kernel /boot/vmlinuz-2.6.0-test2 root=/dev/hda3
boot

after I use:
root (hd0,2)
kernel /boot/vmlinuz-2.6.0-test2 root=/dev/sda2
boot

sda1, sda2, sda4 but any success, same mistake...

> If that isn't the problem, then make sure the root file system is built into the kernel config -- and in this case, also IDE support.

I'm send my .config for you look.

> Cheers,
> -Len

Thank's for attention.

